{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>If.</b> Like the accent of כי, or its meaning is 'holy'—it says concerning the remnant: if HaShem washes thus from Zion." "<b>Will rinse.</b> Like יָדִיחוּ אֶת־הָעֹלָה (Ezekiel 40:38), like 'they will wash.'" "<b>A spirit of burning.</b> From the root of וּבִעַרְתָּ הָרָע (Deuteronomy 21:21)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase טעמו קדוש is obscure; read hyper-literally as 'its meaning is holy.' The syntax of the second clause is difficult and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:02.901639301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}